                <pb facs="0094" n="9" sameAs="frus:frus1919v02/pg9"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">837.00/1516: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Cuba</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Gonzales</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Habana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1919-02-15T10:00:00-05:29"><hi rendition="#italic">February 15,
                                1919, 10 a.m.</hi></date><lb/>[<hi rendition="#italic">Received 1.13
                            p.m.</hi>]</dateline></opener>
                <p>69. My February 12th, 11 a.m. and February 13th, 2 p.m. Statement given to press
                    today. The President anxious to have General Crowder come at once as present
                    Congress is agitating election reform law.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Gonzales</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
